    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0473" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/10–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-27T16:00:00+03:25">October 27, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 27—1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>786. Tudeh (masses) Party<anchor n="73" xml:id="d494-f1"/> started mass
                    demonstration today in front of Majlis demanding ouster of Saed government.
                    While crowd has been estimated as high as 35,000 persons it was completely
                    orderly and though a great quantity of Iranian armed troops, tanks, et cetera
                    appeared there have been no incidents as far as Embassy is aware. Some Soviet
                    troops armed with Tommy guns were present and Soviet sponsorship of the
                    demonstration cannot be questioned.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d494-f1" n="73" xml:id="d494-f1-content">
                <p>Iranian Communist Party.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
